%% ============================================================
%%  PROFILE & BALANCE SEQUENCE DIAGRAMS
%%  Co-Working Space Application
%%  Scenarios: Balance, Username, Password, Email, Phone
%% ============================================================


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 12 — View Balance and Transaction History
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Diagram 12 — View Balance and Transaction History

    User->>App: Navigate to Balance tab
    App->>Storage: Read auth_token
    Storage-->>App: JWT token

    par Fetch user profile (balance)
        App->>+API: GET /me
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        API->>DB: Fetch user record by token
        DB-->>API: User data with current balance
        API-->>-App: 200 — {name, email, balance, ...}
        App-->>User: Display current balance card
    and Fetch transaction history
        App->>+API: GET /me/balance-history
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        API->>DB: Fetch all balance transactions for user
        DB-->>API: List of transactions
        API-->>-App: 200 — [{type, amount, room, date, ...}]
        App->>App: Parse and convert timestamps to local timezone
        App-->>User: Display transaction history list
    end

    alt Token expired
        API-->>-App: 401 — Unauthorized
        App-->>User: Show session expired error
    end


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 13 — Manual Balance Recharge (CCP / Algérie Poste)
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Clipboard as Clipboard Service
    participant CCP as Algérie Poste (External)
    participant Email as Company Email
    participant Admin as Admin Panel
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Diagram 13 — Manual Balance Recharge (Offline Flow)

    User->>App: View Balance screen recharge instructions
    App-->>User: Display CCP account details card
    Note right of App: Shows: account number, name, address, RIP

    User->>App: Tap copy icon next to account number
    App->>Clipboard: Copy account number to clipboard
    Clipboard-->>App: Copied
    App-->>User: Show "Copied to clipboard" confirmation

    User->>CCP: Perform money transfer via postal account
    CCP-->>User: Transfer receipt issued

    User->>Email: Send payment receipt to company email
    Note right of User: Email provided in the app instructions

    Admin->>Admin: Verify payment receipt manually
    Admin->>+API: POST /admin/users/f_balance/{user_uid}
    Note right of Admin: Body: {balance: amount}
    API->>DB: Add credited amount to user balance
    DB-->>API: Balance updated
    API-->>-Admin: 200 — Balance updated

    Note over User,DB: User sees updated balance on next app open or refresh


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 14 — View Account Settings (Profile)
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Diagram 14 — View Account Settings

    User->>App: Navigate to Account tab → Account Settings
    App->>Storage: Read auth_token + auth_provider + has_password flag
    Storage-->>App: Stored credentials metadata

    App->>+API: GET /me
    Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
    API->>DB: Fetch complete user profile
    DB-->>API: {name, email, phone, has_password, ...}

    alt Token invalid or expired
        API-->>-App: 401 — Unauthorized
        App-->>User: Show session expired error
    else User not found
        API-->>-App: 404 — User not found
        App-->>User: Show account error
    else Success
        API-->>-App: 200 — Full profile data
        App->>App: Populate name, email, phone fields
        App->>App: Determine auth mode (local vs Google)
        App-->>User: Display profile: avatar, name, email, phone
        Note right of App: Password field shows "Set a password" for Google users
    end


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 15 — Update Username
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Diagram 15 — Update Username

    User->>App: Tap edit icon next to Name field
    App-->>User: Show "Change Username" dialog
    Note right of App: Dialog pre-filled with current username

    User->>App: Enter new username
    App->>App: Validate: non-empty, different from current

    alt Username is empty
        App-->>User: Show empty field error
    else Username unchanged
        App-->>User: Dismiss dialog — no request sent
    else Valid new username
        User->>App: Tap Save
        App->>Storage: Read auth_token
        Storage-->>App: JWT token

        App->>+API: PUT /me
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        Note right of App: Body: {username: newUsername}

        API->>DB: Update username for authenticated user

        alt Token invalid or expired
            DB-->>API: Auth failure
            API-->>-App: 401 — Session expired
            App-->>User: Show session expired error
        else User not found
            API-->>-App: 404 — User not found
            App-->>User: Show account error
        else Username updated successfully
            DB-->>API: Update confirmed
            API-->>-App: 200 — Profile updated
            App->>App: Update userName reactive variable
            App-->>User: Show success notification
            App-->>User: Avatar initial and name field refresh instantly
        end
    end


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 16 — Change Password (Local Account)
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Diagram 16 — Change Password (Local Account)

    User->>App: Tap edit icon next to Password field
    App-->>User: Show "Change Password" dialog
    Note right of App: Fields: current password, new password, confirm

    User->>App: Fill in all password fields
    App->>App: Validate: no empty fields, passwords match, min 8 chars

    alt Validation failed
        App-->>User: Show corresponding validation error
    else All validations pass
        User->>App: Tap Save
        App->>Storage: Read auth_token
        Storage-->>App: JWT token

        App->>+API: PUT /me/password
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        Note right of App: Body: {old_password, new_password}

        API->>DB: Verify old password hash

        alt Old password incorrect
            DB-->>API: Hash mismatch
            API-->>-App: 401 — Wrong current password
            App-->>User: Show wrong password error
        else Token expired
            API-->>-App: 401 — Session expired
            App-->>User: Show session expired error
        else User not found
            API-->>-App: 404 — User not found
            App-->>User: Show account error
        else Password updated
            DB->>DB: Hash and store new password
            DB-->>API: Password updated
            API-->>-App: 200 — Password changed successfully
            App->>Storage: Write has_password = true
            App-->>User: Show success notification
        end
    end


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 17 — Change Email Address (2-Step Flow)
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database
    participant Mail as Email Service

    Note over User,Mail: Diagram 17 — Change Email Address (2-Step Flow)

    Note over User,Mail: Step 1 — Request Email Change

    User->>App: Tap edit icon next to Email field
    App-->>User: Navigate to Email Change screen
    User->>App: Enter new email address

    App->>Storage: Read auth_token
    Storage-->>App: JWT token

    App->>+API: POST /me/email/request
    Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
    Note right of App: Body: {new_email}

    API->>DB: Check if new email is already in use

    alt Email already registered
        DB-->>API: Email conflict
        API-->>-App: 409 — Email already used
        App-->>User: Show email already taken error
    else Email service failure
        API-->>-App: 500 — Failed to send verification email
        App-->>User: Show service error — try again later
    else Email is available
        DB-->>API: Email is free
        API->>Mail: Send 6-digit OTP to new email address
        Mail-->>User: OTP email delivered to new address
        API-->>-App: 200 — Verification code sent
        App-->>User: Show OTP input screen

        Note over User,API: Step 2 — Confirm Email Change

        User->>App: Enter 6-digit OTP code
        App->>+API: POST /me/email/confirm
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        Note right of App: Body: {code}

        API->>DB: Validate OTP against pending request

        alt No pending request found
            DB-->>API: No pending change
            API-->>-App: 400 — No pending email change request
            App-->>User: Show expired request error
        else OTP invalid
            DB-->>API: Code mismatch
            API-->>-App: 401 — Invalid verification code
            App-->>User: Show wrong code error
        else OTP valid
            DB->>DB: Update user email address
            DB-->>API: Email updated
            API-->>-App: 200 — Email changed successfully
            App-->>User: Show success and navigate back to settings
        end
    end


%% ============================================================
%%  DIAGRAM 18 — Add / Change Phone Number (2-Step Flow)
%% ============================================================

sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as Mobile App
    participant Storage as Secure Storage
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as Database
    participant SMS as SMS Service

    Note over User,SMS: Diagram 18 — Add / Change Phone Number (2-Step Flow)

    Note over User,SMS: Step 1 — Send Verification Code

    User->>App: Tap Verify or Change on Phone field
    App-->>User: Navigate to Phone Verification screen
    User->>App: Enter phone number

    App->>Storage: Read auth_token
    Storage-->>App: JWT token

    App->>+API: POST /me/phone/send-code
    Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
    Note right of App: Body: {phone}

    API->>DB: Check if phone already linked to another account

    alt Phone already used by another account
        DB-->>API: Phone conflict
        API-->>-App: 409 — Phone number already in use
        App-->>User: Show phone already taken error
    else User not found
        API-->>-App: 404 — User not found
        App-->>User: Show account error
    else Phone available
        DB-->>API: Phone is free
        API->>SMS: Send 6-digit OTP via SMS
        SMS-->>User: SMS OTP delivered
        API-->>-App: 200 — SMS code sent
        App-->>User: Show OTP input screen

        Note over User,API: Step 2 — Verify SMS Code

        User->>App: Enter 6-digit SMS code
        App->>+API: POST /me/phone/verify-code
        Note right of App: Header: Authorization Bearer token
        Note right of App: Body: {phone, code}

        API->>DB: Validate OTP against pending entry

        alt No pending code for this number
            DB-->>API: No pending verification
            API-->>-App: 400 — No pending code found
            App-->>User: Show expired code error — request again
        else Code belongs to a different user
            DB-->>API: Code ownership mismatch
            API-->>-App: 403 — Code belongs to a different user
            App-->>User: Show ownership error
        else OTP invalid
            DB-->>API: Code mismatch
            API-->>-App: 401 — Invalid SMS code
            App-->>User: Show wrong code error
        else OTP valid
            DB->>DB: Link phone number to user account
            DB-->>API: Phone verified and saved
            API-->>-App: 200 — Phone number verified
            App-->>User: Show success and navigate back to settings
        end
    end
